1
00:00:00,958 --> 00:00:03,208
(Amy:)Which word's tripping you up?

2
00:00:03,419 --> 00:00:05,299
Assuage or aItruism?

3
00:00:07,047 --> 00:00:08,877
(Penny:)Both.

4
00:00:09,466 --> 00:00:12,056
(Bernadette:)You'll feel better
by doing something nice for someone.

5
00:00:12,261 --> 00:00:15,181
- Oh, I actually knew that.
- I never doubted you.

6
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:18,770
(Bernadette:)Every other week,
I serve at a soup kitchen downtown.

7
00:00:18,976 --> 00:00:20,936
(Penny:)Ooh. I can't do that.

8
00:00:21,145 --> 00:00:23,855
(Penny:)If I stand over a steaming pot,
my hair just goes: "Boing!"

9
00:00:25,607 --> 00:00:28,027
- Ah. What else can I do?
- There's Habitat for Humanity.

10
00:00:28,235 --> 00:00:29,735
(Amy:)Building houses for the poor.

11
00:00:29,945 --> 00:00:33,235
I don't have my own house,
I'm gonna build one for someone else?

12
00:00:34,324 --> 00:00:36,704
(Amy:)How about donating
some of your clothes?

13
00:00:37,619 --> 00:00:41,249
Oh, my God, that's perfect, because
I have so many clothes I don't wear.

14
00:00:41,457 --> 00:00:43,787
They're taking up space
I go shopping to buy more.

15
00:00:44,001 --> 00:00:46,291
(Penny:)I have no place to put it.
This would fix that.

16
00:00:46,503 --> 00:00:50,213
- What about helping people?
- And helping people.

17
00:00:52,676 --> 00:00:54,306
- Here's your cocoa.
- Oh.

18
00:00:54,511 --> 00:00:56,851
- HaIf and haIf instead of whole milk?
- Yes.

19
00:00:57,055 --> 00:00:59,145
- Heated to precisely 183 degrees?
- Yes.

20
00:00:59,349 --> 00:01:02,099
(Sheldon:)Seven little marshmallows,
no more, no less?

